    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Weakness, numbness of the ring and little fingers, and curling of those fingers in the right hand for four weeks after a fall onto the right elbow, in a left-handed artist who uses the right hand for the palette and brushwork; stroke and a peripheral nerve lesion under evaluation</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R29.818</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting concern; it echoes, without asserting, the paralysis of his right hand recorded later in 1517 (CLM-0006). Superseded by the diagnosis at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>One fall in the past year (slipped on stone stairs and landed on the right elbow), with no loss of consciousness, dizziness, or palpitations before it; fall risk</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z91.81</td><td>S — Synthetic fall that anchors the modern ulnar nerve injury; no historical fall is asserted.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

