<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Weakness, numbness of the ring and little fingers, and curling of those fingers in the right hand for four weeks after a fall onto the right elbow, in a left-handed artist who uses the right hand for the palette and brushwork; stroke and a peripheral nerve lesion under evaluation: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>One fall in the past year (slipped on stone stairs and landed on the right elbow), with no loss of consciousness, dizziness, or palpitations before it; fall risk: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Same-day assessment for stroke and localization: full neurological examination and NIH Stroke Scale, MRI of the brain with diffusion-weighted imaging, X-ray of the right elbow, and an ECG. Guideline: Cubital Tunnel Syndrome (Ulnar Nerve Entrapment at the Elbow), OrthoInfo (2026); Treatment for ulnar neuropathy at the elbow (Caliandro P, et al.) (2025); Practice parameter for electrodiagnostic studies in ulnar neuropathy at the elbow: summary statement (American Association of Electrodiagnostic Medicine, American Academy of Neurology, American Academy of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation) (1999); 2021 Guideline for the Prevention of Stroke in Patients With Stroke and Transient Ischemic Attack: A Guideline From the American Heart Association/American Stroke Association (2021) [S]</item><item>Hand surgery consultation with nerve conduction studies, EMG, and ultrasound of the ulnar nerve, to confirm the site and severity and to advise on splinting, hand therapy, and surgery. Guideline: Cubital Tunnel Syndrome (Ulnar Nerve Entrapment at the Elbow), OrthoInfo (2026); Treatment for ulnar neuropathy at the elbow (Caliandro P, et al.) (2025); Practice parameter for electrodiagnostic studies in ulnar neuropathy at the elbow: summary statement (American Association of Electrodiagnostic Medicine, American Academy of Neurology, American Academy of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation) (1999) [S]</item><item>Protect the nerve now: no leaning on the right elbow (a gel elbow pad and a padded armrest at the drawing table), avoid prolonged elbow bending, a towel loosely wrapped around the elbow at night until a splint is made; acetaminophen for pain. Guideline: Cubital Tunnel Syndrome (Ulnar Nerve Entrapment at the Elbow), OrthoInfo (2026); Treatment for ulnar neuropathy at the elbow (Caliandro P, et al.) (2025); Practice parameter for electrodiagnostic studies in ulnar neuropathy at the elbow: summary statement (American Association of Electrodiagnostic Medicine, American Academy of Neurology, American Academy of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation) (1999) [S]</item><item>Stroke risk-factor screen: blood pressure at every visit with a week of home readings, lipid panel with lipoprotein(a), HbA1c, ECG, and pulse check for atrial fibrillation. Guideline: 2021 Guideline for the Prevention of Stroke in Patients With Stroke and Transient Ischemic Attack: A Guideline From the American Heart Association/American Stroke Association (2021); 2019 ACC/AHA Guideline on the Primary Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease (2019); 2018 AHA/ACC/AACVPR/AAPA/ABC/ACPM/ADA/AGS/APhA/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline on the Management of Blood Cholesterol (2018); Statin Use for the Primary Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease in Adults: Preventive Medication (2022); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hyperlipidemia monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Falls: a handrail on both sides of the stone staircase, night lighting, footwear review, and a Timed Up and Go at the wellness visit. Guideline: Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>
